    <string name="how_to_create_wa_backup">Step 1: On the phone open WhatsApp → Settings → Chats → Chat backup → tap “Back Up” (choose “On device”, Google Drive OFF is fine). Step 2: Grant this app all-files access (or pick the WhatsApp folder) so it can read Android/media/com.whatsapp/…/.Backups/msgstore-*.crypt14. Step 3: Press “Backup now”. The .crypt14 file stays encrypted by WhatsApp AND is additionally AES-encrypted before upload — only you with the token+passphrase can decrypt it.</string>
    <string name="label_auto_mode">Auto mode (no server): collect chats to Documents/wa-auto, pull to PC over USB</string>
